+++ b/ui/UPSTREAM.md
@@ -0,0 +1,38 @@
+# JetKVM frontend for webOS
+
+This directory contains the patched UI source from https://github.com/jetkvm/kvm
+at release/0.5.9, commit `36c008fb5cc209f9f9f149ab4e9a864ec7d72cad`.
+The upstream Go/device firmware is not built or required. The source archive
+includes `internal/logging/sse.html`, the target of upstream's public-page symlink.
+Fonts, icons, font preloads, title, colors, and theme behavior are retained
+from this pinned upstream revision.
+
+The frontend and webOS integration in this directory are distributed under
+GNU GPL version 2; see LICENSE. Original copyright notices are preserved.
+Modified upstream files carry a dated modification notice.
+
+The port retains JetKVM's WebRTCVideo, ActionBar, virtual keyboard, paste dialog,
+macro editor, appearance/keyboard settings, charts, components, styles and fonts.
+`src/webos/` mounts the upstream WebSocket signaling hook, attaches the standard
+JSON-RPC and HID RPC v1 channels, and supplies the TV remote and console entry
+point. `src/hooks/useJsonRpc.ts`, `useHidRpc.ts`, and `useKeyboard.ts` are upstream
+source. The signaling hook has only a TypeScript interop annotation; its wire
+protocol is unchanged. The native server translates JetKVM reports into TV input
+and saves keyboard layout/macros. Existing browser macros migrate once without
+overwriting saved TV console preferences. USB storage, extension controls,
+cloud management, and JetKVM device configuration are omitted from this port.
+Encoder presets and other server settings belong to the TV setup app. Keep
+the browser frontend focused on the upstream console components and stream
+statistics; do not add encoder configuration pages here.
+
+The parent repository pins the unmodified upstream in `third_party/jetkvm` and
+carries the webOS integration in `patches/jetkvm/series`.
+`npm run build:ui` in the parent prepares this directory under `build/jetkvm/ui`,
+installs its locked dependencies, and builds the frontend. Edit the generated
+source and run `npm run refresh:ui-patch` in the parent to refresh the webOS patch.
+
+The source archive served by the TV contains this complete patched frontend,
+plus the patch series and upstream revision. To build this standalone source,
+run `npm ci --ignore-scripts` and `npm run build:device` in this directory.
+The parent build stages the static assets separately from the native server,
+with this license, third-party notices, and the complete modified UI source.
